%abstract=<begin abstract english> Let $\pi \colon  Y\to X$ be a finite composition of blow-ups of smooth complex projective varieties along smooth centres of codimension at least three. We prove that a finite-index subgroup of $\Aut  (Y)$ descends faithfully to $\Aut  (X)$. In particular, such blow-ups cannot turn a finite automorphism group into an infinite one. For a blow-up with connected nonempty centre, the numerical pullback space is a hyperplane on which the Hessian determinant of the top intersection form vanishes. <end abstract english>
